    "### 1. Stereographic Projection Chart\n",
    "For the unit circle $S^1 = \\{(x, y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : x^2 + y^2 = 1\\}$, excluding the north pole $N = (0, 1)$:\n",
    "The projection maps a point $P=(x, y)$ to the intersection of the line passing through $N$ and $P$ with the $x$-axis.\n",
    "Equation of line: $Y - 1 = \\frac{y-1}{x} X$.\n",
    "Setting $Y=0$:\n",
    "$$X = \\frac{-x}{y-1} = \\frac{x}{1-y}$$\n",
    "So the chart map is:\n",
    "$$\\phi(x, y) = \\frac{x}{1-y}$$\n",
    "The inverse chart map $\\phi^{-1}(u)$ is:\n",
    "$$x = \\frac{2u}{u^2+1}, \\quad y = \\frac{u^2-1}{u^2+1}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Chart formulas verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Rotation Vector to Rotation Matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def rodrigues_formula(omega):\n",
    "    theta = np.linalg.norm(omega)\n",
    "    if theta < 1e-8:\n",
    "        return np.eye(3)\n",
    "    u = omega / theta\n",
    "    # Skew-symmetric matrix\n",
    "    K = np.array([\n",
    "        [0, -u[2], u[1]],\n",
    "        [u[2], 0, -u[0]],\n",
    "        [-u[1], u[0], 0]\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    R = np.eye(3) + np.sin(theta) * K + (1 - np.cos(theta)) * (K @ K)\n",
    "    return R\n",
    "\n",
    "R = rodrigues_formula([0.1, 0.2, 0.3])\n",
    "print(\"R:\\n\", R)\n",
    "print(\"Is orthogonal (R^T R - I):\\n\", np.abs(R.T @ R - np.eye(3)) < 1e-9)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Fisher Information of a Bernoulli Distribution\n",
    "$$\\log p(x; \\theta) = x \\log \\theta + (1-x) \\log(1-\\theta)$$\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial \\log p}{\\partial \\theta} = \\frac{x}{\\theta} - \\frac{1-x}{1-\\theta}$$\n",
    "Fisher Information is the variance of the score function:\n",
    "$$F(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}\\left[ \\left( \\frac{x}{\\theta} - \\frac{1-x}{1-\\theta} \\right)^2 \\right]$$\n",
    "Since $X \\sim \\text{Bernoulli}(\\theta)$, $x^2=x$:\n",
    "$$F(\\theta) = \\frac{\\theta}{\\theta^2} + \\frac{1-\\theta}{(1-\\theta)^2} = \\frac{1}{\\theta} + \\frac{1}{1-\\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\theta(1-\\theta)}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical derivation verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. Tangent Vectors of a Sphere\n",
    "The unit sphere is defined by $f(\\mathbf{x}) = x_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 - 1 = 0$.\n",
    "The tangent space at $p$ is orthogonal to the gradient of the constraint function: $\\nabla f(p) = 2p$.\n",
    "For $p = [0, 0, 1]^T$, the tangent space is all vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ such that $p^T \\mathbf{v} = 0$, i.e. $v_3 = 0$.\n",
    "A basis for $T_p S^2$ is:\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{e}_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{e}_2 = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Basis vectors verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. Christoffel Symbols Derivation\n",
    "Christoffel symbols of the second kind represent the connection (how vector fields are parallel transported). They are defined as:\n",
    "$$\\Gamma_{ij}^k = \\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{l} g^{kl} \\left( \\frac{\\partial g_{jl}}{\\partial x^i} + \\frac{\\partial g_{il}}{\\partial x^j} - \\frac{\\partial g_{ij}}{\\partial x^l} \\right)$$\n",
    "where $g^{kl}$ is the inverse of the metric tensor matrix $g_{kl}$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Formula verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Poincaré Half-Plane Metric\n",
    "The metric tensor matrix is:\n",
    "$$g(x, y) = \\begin{bmatrix} \\frac{1}{y^2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{y^2} \\end{bmatrix}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Metric tensor verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
